Usages:
  branding_pattern: |
    Values are branded via `toBrandedType` (a phantom-type cast with no runtime effect) so that
    plain primitives (numbers, tuples, objects) gain a nominal type tag (e.g. a geometry point
    vs. a plain [number, number] tuple) that the TypeScript compiler can distinguish. Use it when
    a value must be treated as a distinct type from its underlying representation, never to
    perform any actual data transformation.
  env_detection: |
    Use isTestEnv/isDevEnv/isProdEnv-style checks (based on import.meta.env.MODE) instead
    of hardcoding environment-specific behavior; this keeps deterministic IDs and other
    test-only branches isolated to the test environment.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the shared low-level utility foundation of the whole monorepo: it has no
  rendering or scene logic of its own and no dependency on any other cell in this forest. It
  provides generic data-structure primitives (heap, event emitter, versioned snapshot store),
  environment detection, the color system, keyboard-key constants/matching, id/random
  generation, and a large set of array/object helper functions consumed by every other cell.

  Use `branding_pattern` when a function here produces a value another cell will treat as a
  nominal type (this is how packages/math/src builds its geometry types on top of this cell's
  `toBrandedType`).

---

"Emitter()":
  location: emitter.ts
  annotations: |
    Generic typed publish/subscribe channel. Holds an ordered list of subscriber callbacks;
    trigger invokes every current subscriber synchronously with the same payload tuple T.
    Used throughout the codebase (scene updates, store increments, history changes) as the
    common event-notification primitive.
  properties:
    "subscribers -> Array<(...payload: T) => void>": |
      Currently registered subscriber callbacks, in registration order.
  methods:
    "on(...handlers: Array<Function>) -> unsubscribe:Function": |
      Register one or more handlers; returns a callback that removes exactly the handlers
      registered by this call.
    "once(...handlers: Array<Function>) -> unsubscribe:Function": |
      Like on, but each handler is automatically removed after its first invocation.
    "off(...handlers: Array<Function>)": |
      Remove previously registered handlers.
    "trigger(...payload: T)": |
      Synchronously invoke every current subscriber with `payload`.
    "clear()": |
      Remove all subscribers.

"BinaryHeap<T>(scoreFunction: Function)":
  location: binary-heap.ts
  annotations: |
    Generic binary min-heap ordered by `scoreFunction`. Used where a data structure needs
    efficient repeated access to the lowest-scored element (e.g. priority-ordered processing).
  methods:
    "push(node: T)": |
      Insert `node`, restoring heap order.
    "pop() -> node:T | null": |
      Remove and return the lowest-scored node, or `null` if empty.
    "remove(node: T)": |
      Remove a specific node (by reference equality) from anywhere in the heap.
    "size() -> count:number": |
      Number of nodes currently in the heap.
    "rescoreElement(node: T)": |
      Re-position `node` after its score has changed externally.

"VersionedSnapshotStore<T>(initialValue: T)":
  location: versionedSnapshotStore.ts
  annotations: |
    Tiny observable store: wraps a value of type T with an incrementing version number,
    supporting both push (subscribe) and pull (pull, long-poll-style await-next-version)
    consumption. Used where a value changes over time and different consumers need either
    immediate notification or an on-demand "wait for the next change" primitive.
  methods:
    "getSnapshot() -> snapshot:{ version: number, value: T }": |
      Return the current version/value pair.
    "set(nextValue: T) -> changed:boolean": |
      Replace the value (per the configured equality check); bumps the version and notifies
      subscribers only if the value actually changed.
    "update(updater: Function) -> changed:boolean": |
      Compute the next value from the previous one, then behave like set.
    "subscribe(subscriber: Function) -> unsubscribe:Function": |
      Register a callback invoked on every future version bump.
    "pull(sinceVersion: number) -> next:Promise<{ version: number, value: T }>": |
      Resolve as soon as the store's version exceeds `sinceVersion` (immediately if it already
      does), with the snapshot at that point.

"arrayToMap(items: Array<{ id: string }> | Map<string, any>) -> map:Map<string, any>":
  location: utils.ts
  annotations: |
    Convert an array of objects with an id field (or a Map already) into a Map keyed by
    id. Used everywhere an element/entity list needs O(1) id lookup.

"toBrandedType(value: any) -> branded:any":
  location: utils.ts
  annotations: |
    Cast `value` to a nominally-branded type with no runtime transformation.

    `value`: the plain representation to brand
    `branded`: the same value, now typed as the requested branded type

    Use `branding_pattern` for when and why to call this.

"debounce(fn: Function, timeout: number) -> debounced:Function":
  location: utils.ts
  annotations: |
    Standard trailing-edge debounce wrapper; the returned function also exposes flush()
    (run any pending call immediately) and cancel() (drop any pending call).

"randomId() -> id:string":
  location: random.ts
  annotations: |
    Generate a new unique id (nanoid-based). Under isTestEnv, returns deterministic
    sequential ids (id0, id1, ...) instead, so snapshot tests stay stable.

    Use `env_detection` for the test/non-test branching this function relies on.

"matchKey(event: KeyboardEvent, key: string) -> matches:boolean":
  location: keys.ts
  annotations: |
    Test whether a keyboard event corresponds to a named logical key from the shared KEYS
    table (which normalizes platform differences, e.g. CTRL_OR_CMD resolves to metaKey on
    macOS and ctrlKey elsewhere).

    `event`: the keyboard event to test
    `key`: a key from the KEYS constant table
    `matches`: whether `event` represents that logical key

"isColorDark(color: string, threshold: number) -> dark:boolean":
  location: colors.ts
  annotations: |
    Compute perceptual brightness of `color` and compare it against `threshold` to decide
    whether light or dark foreground content should be drawn on top of it. Part of the shared
    color system alongside the COLOR_PALETTE constant table and dark-mode filter helpers.

